# MagTapp Pro - prototype API walkthrough
#
# Run top to bottom. The story is steps 3 -> 5 -> 6: the same request, from the
# same client, returns 403 and then 200, with nothing changing except a row in
# the database that only the server can write.
#
# Setup:
#   cp .env.example .env
#   npm install
#   npm run seed
#   npm start
#
# VS Code REST Client / JetBrains HTTP Client both run this file. The @token
# variables are captured from earlier responses.

@host = http://localhost:4000


### 1. Sign in as a free user. Creates the account on first call.
# @name authFree
POST {{host}}/v1/auth
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "free@example.com" }

@freeToken = {{authFree.response.body.token}}


### 2. Entitlement before paying. tier is "free"; documents is locked.
# Expect 200:
# { "tier": "free",
#   "features": {
#     "documents": { "tier": "pro" },
#     "translate": { "tier": "free", "limit": 5, "used": 0 } } }
GET {{host}}/v1/me/entitlement
Authorization: Bearer {{freeToken}}


### 3. THE POINT OF THE PROTOTYPE - free user hits the Pro endpoint.
# Expect 403 PRO_REQUIRED. No client-side flag can change this.
GET {{host}}/v1/ai/documents
Authorization: Bearer {{freeToken}}


### 4. Free metered feature. Works 5 times today, 429 on the 6th.
GET {{host}}/v1/ai/translate
Authorization: Bearer {{freeToken}}


### 4b. A fabricated receipt is refused. Expect 422 INVALID_RECEIPT.
POST {{host}}/v1/subscriptions/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{freeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "platform": "android", "purchaseToken": "i_made_this_up", "productId": "pro_monthly" }


### 5. Subscribe. Any token starting with "valid_" is treated as a real purchase.
# Expect 200 with status "active" and currentPeriodEnd 30 days out.
POST {{host}}/v1/subscriptions/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{freeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "platform": "android", "purchaseToken": "valid_alice_001", "productId": "pro_monthly" }


### 6. Same request as step 3, same token. Now 200.
# Nothing about the client changed. Entitlement was re-derived server-side.
GET {{host}}/v1/ai/documents
Authorization: Bearer {{freeToken}}


### 7. Entitlement now reads "pro", and translate's limit is null (unlimited).
GET {{host}}/v1/me/entitlement
Authorization: Bearer {{freeToken}}


### 8. Re-sending the same receipt is idempotent - no second subscription,
# no extra 30 days. Apps retry on flaky networks and this must be a no-op.
POST {{host}}/v1/subscriptions/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{freeToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "platform": "android", "purchaseToken": "valid_alice_001", "productId": "pro_monthly" }


### 9. Second user, for the receipt-sharing test.
# @name authOther
POST {{host}}/v1/auth
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "mallory@example.com" }

@otherToken = {{authOther.response.body.token}}


### 10. ANTI-SHARING - Mallory pastes Alice's receipt.
# Expect 409 RECEIPT_ALREADY_CLAIMED. One purchase, one account, enforced by a
# unique index on originalTransactionId.
POST {{host}}/v1/subscriptions/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{otherToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "platform": "android", "purchaseToken": "valid_alice_001", "productId": "pro_monthly" }


### 11. Webhook: renewal. Extends currentPeriodEnd by 30 days.
# Real equivalents: Apple posts App Store Server Notifications V2 directly;
# Google publishes Real-Time Developer Notifications via Pub/Sub.
POST {{host}}/v1/webhooks/mock
Content-Type: application/json

{ "originalTransactionId": "otx_alice_001", "eventType": "renewed", "notificationId": "notif_001" }


### 12. IDEMPOTENCY - the exact same notification again.
# Expect 200 { "deduplicated": true }. No second 30 days granted.
# Stores retry when they don't get a prompt 2xx, so this case is routine.
POST {{host}}/v1/webhooks/mock
Content-Type: application/json

{ "originalTransactionId": "otx_alice_001", "eventType": "renewed", "notificationId": "notif_001" }


### 13. Webhook: expiry. Sets status to expired.
POST {{host}}/v1/webhooks/mock
Content-Type: application/json

{ "originalTransactionId": "otx_alice_001", "eventType": "expired", "notificationId": "notif_002" }


### 14. Access is gone immediately. Expect 403 PRO_REQUIRED again.
# Nothing ran to revoke it - no job, no flag flipped. The entitlement rule just
# stopped returning true, which is the argument for deriving it.
GET {{host}}/v1/ai/documents
Authorization: Bearer {{freeToken}}


### 15. Unauthenticated request. Expect 401 UNAUTHORIZED.
GET {{host}}/v1/me/entitlement
